      en: "Starčeva Gorica Monastery is located on an island in Lake Skadar. Founded in the 14th century, it is dedicated to the Dormition of the Theotokos. The monastery was a center for monasticism and prayer. It was destroyed by the Ottomans in 1470. The current church was built in 1710. The island has an area of 2 hectares. The monastery is known for its olive groves. It is accessible only by boat. Today, it houses a community of nuns.",
