      en: "Upper Vrmac Fortress (Vrmac Gornja) is located on Mount Vrmac above Tivat in the Bay of Kotor. Built in the 19th century by the Austrians to defend the bay, the fortress is part of a larger defensive system on Vrmac. It consists of a central battery with gun platforms and surrounding ditches. The fortress saw combat in World War I. After World War II it was abandoned. Today it is a popular destination for hikers who climb from the sea. From the fortress, there is a wide view over the Bay of Kotor and the surrounding mountains. The structure is well-preserved but overgrown.",
